E2BC                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
E2BC                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (60h) is
E2BC                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
