E36C                          IF   CHECKED   
E36C                             ; The checked build's inner loop, out of page 1, where it would not fit,
E36C                             ; and its break check (described with the unchecked one in page 1).
E36C                             ; pnext: the break check, then (falling through) next. A word call, a true
E36C                             ; "(" and a true ")" end here, but the keyboard is looked at only once in 256
E36C                             ; of them: CDOWN counts them down. A key found is held; a Ctrl-C goes on to ctlc. (Startup
E36C                             ; falls in here too, which does no harm.)
E36C   CE 79 04     PNEXT:    DEC   CDOWN   
E36F   D0 0F                  BNE   next   
E371   20 06 FF               JSR   KEY   
E374   F0 0A                  BEQ   next   ; no key
E376   8D 7A 04               STA   KEYBUF   ; held for the next "?"
E379   C9 03                  CMP   #3   
