E619                             ; lcol: the line (D0/D1) and the column (T1/T2) of the place at P, both from
E619                             ; 1. A place below the program is in the -n? line buffer: line 0, and the
E619                             ; column is the place in the buffer. Otherwise the LFs before the place are
E619                             ; counted from PROG; T1/T2 holds the address before the line's first
E619                             ; character (the last LF, or PROG - 1), and the column is P minus that.
E619   A0 00        LCOL:     LDY   #0   
